# IRW: Inter Register Write - 8-bit mask instruction
# YAML: mask "1111_1111_1000_0000", opcode "153400" (octal)
# Writes A register to specified register on specified privilege level
#
# P-code implementation:
# write_register_to_level(level, register, A);
#
# SLEIGH implementation handles level and register selection
:IRW level, reg_dst is op8=0xD6 & level & reg_dst {
    # Inter-level register access (simplified)
    # In real hardware, this writes to register bank for specific privilege level
    # For analysis purposes, treat as register copy with privilege annotation
    reg_dst = A;

    # Note: Full implementation would require privilege level checking
    # and access to different register contexts per level
}